  <h2>Method matters as much as the headline time</h2>
  <p>An operator can approve a request quickly while the payment rail adds more time. Compare the full path: identity review, operator processing and final delivery. A published “processing” estimate is not necessarily the time until funds arrive.</p>
  <h2>Minimums can change the best option</h2>
  <p>Method-specific thresholds matter for smaller balances. McLuck publishes different minimums for bank transfer and gift cards, while Stake.us publishes a 40 SC minimum and Dorados publishes 100 SC. Always confirm the live cashier before playing toward a target.</p>
